{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-27 08:24:44 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-27 15:24:44 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\n## Pending-link failure policy — owner decision brief\n\n**Decision:** Who ends a link when its content source never answers? M5 currently leaves the link pending without a deadline. At the REPL, the pending run retains subsequent input until the link completes or the caller uses `(abandon)`.\n\n| Option | Decision and change | Cost |\n|---|---|---|\n| **A — Keep the current behavior permanently** | The linker stays clock-free. A caller that wants a deadline composes `dao.lease` and calls `abandon` when its lease lapses. | No linker work now; every caller owns its timeout policy indefinitely. |\n| **B — Add a lease per pending link now** | Wire lease grants, renewals, ticks, judging, and reclaim into linker operation. | A new dependency and lease bookkeeping for every pending link, including callers that want to wait indefinitely. |\n| **C — Defer, with a documented composition hook** | Keep M5 behavior and identify the point where a caller’s lease judge would call `abandon`. Implement a deadline when a deployment needs one. | No lease runtime now; documentation and a later implementation decision remain. |\n\n**Current implementation:** M5 implements A’s *behavior*, but the owner has not chosen A as the permanent policy. The [linker design](</Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md>) assigns retry, deadline, and permanent absence to the composition; `fetch` has no deadline. Its section 6.3 already describes the lease seam: the caller renews on progress, and a judge supplied with ticks calls `abandon` on silence. The [lease contract](</Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.lease.md>) requires that judge and its resource reclaim action to live in the possessing composition. A proposed [REPL link-policy design](</Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl.link-policy.md>) describes a configurable hook, but marks it unimplemented.\n\n**Recommendation: C.** Preserve the clock-free linker and document the caller-side `abandon` seam as the decision for now. This follows the existing ownership boundary and avoids imposing lease state on every link before a deployment supplies a deadline, cadence, and recovery needs. When such a deployment exists, its requirements can determine whether a caller-side lease composition suffices. The owner need only rule now that indefinite pending remains the default and that deadlines belong to the composition.\n\nStatus: COMPLETE"}}
